WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.252
Most dashboards have a quiet flaw.

2
00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:06.554
When they can't see something,
they show green anyway.

3
00:00:07.054 --> 00:00:10.284
Argus is my control room,
and it does the opposite.

4
00:00:10.684 --> 00:00:15.498
On every sweep it reads each source: the
clouds, the address book, the code host,

5
00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:16.152
the server.

6
00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:18.317
Each source gets sixty seconds.

7
00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.943
If one fails, Argus keeps its last
good data and marks it stale.

8
00:00:23.443 --> 00:00:26.511
Then twenty-three rules run
against what came back.

9
00:00:26.811 --> 00:00:31.443
Each rule is one file, with its reason
and its exceptions written down.

10
00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:33.043
A rule can pass.

11
00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:35.898
It can break, and name
exactly what broke it.

12
00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:38.803
It can be excepted, on
purpose, with a reason.

13
00:00:39.003 --> 00:00:40.750
Or it can say it could not check.

14
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.922
Watch this source go stale.

15
00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:44.918
Its rules don't stay green.

16
00:00:45.118 --> 00:00:46.210
They turn grey.

17
00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.884
Could not check never counts as a pass.

18
00:00:49.284 --> 00:00:51.734
About three thousand tests hold that line.
